    "recommendations": "• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clear width and overhead clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the main residence and detached structure to keep walls and foundation lines visible to arriving responders.\n• Mark the rear access point with a reflective sign or marker so responders can locate it quickly under low-light or smoky conditions.\n• Keep the rear access gate unlocked or secured with a breakaway latch to allow responders to reach the back of the property without delay.\n• Clear a path between the vehicle parking area and the detached structure wide enough for responders carrying equipment on foot.\n• Trim shrubs and overhanging branches at each access point so responders can move through without obstruction.\n• Keep the walkway between the main residence and detached structure free of stored items, planters, or other objects that could slow foot movement during an emergency.\n• Post the property address in numbers large enough to read from the road, at the access drive entrance."
