    "recommendations": "• Trim branches on large trees that hang directly over or within a few feet of the roof and eaves.\n• Thin the scattered trees nearest to the structure to create more open space between their canopies and the building.\n• Remove shrubs and low plants growing directly against the foundation and exterior walls.\n• Clear brush from the area immediately surrounding the structure, keeping the ground closest to the house as open as possible.\n• Thin or remove shrubs clustered together near the structure to break up the continuous plant material between the brush area and the building.\n• Trim overhanging branches and cut back shrubs along the driveway edges to keep both travel lanes fully clear for vehicles.\n• Mow or cut ground vegetation around the structure and along access routes regularly to keep it short.\n• Remove dead plant material, dry leaves, and loose debris from the ground beneath trees near the structure.\n• Keep both access routes clear of fallen branches and overgrown vegetation so they remain passable.\n• Separate any firewood piles, lumber, or stored materials from the exterior walls of the structure."
